{"step_index":370,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-24T18:59:01Z","input_tokens":3189,"cache_read_tokens":158375,"output_tokens":1466,"thinking":"Identified several matches between data sets, linking specific analytics identifiers to case IDs and associated email addresses: `analytics_901` to `case_04`, `analytics_784` to `case_494`, `analytics_671` to `case_314`, `analytics_5886` to `case_134`, and `analytics_6499` to `case_74`. The next step involves retrieving the corresponding `user_id` for each of these matched deletion requests.\n\n\nExtracted the `user_id` corresponding to `analytics_901` as `user_04` based on the email. Validated a date parsing approach that uses standard Python for speed. The two-pass log correlation process will be examined. An edge case exists: log entries lacking a `trace_id` require special handling, as does the situation where the log line contains a `trace_id`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"python -c \\\"\\nimport glob, json, re\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\n\\nKV_REGEX = re.compile(r'(\\\\w+)=(?:\\\\\\\"([^\\\\\\\"]*)\\\\\\\"|(\\\\S+))')\\n\\nlog_dir = Path(r'C:\\\\Users\\\\Pavan\\\\hackerrank-orchestrate-october26\\\\dataset\\\\evidence\\\\logs')\\ntraces_found = 0\\ncorrelated_rows = 0\\n\\nfor log_file in sorted(log_dir.glob('*.log')):\\n    # trace_id -> list of raw entries (dict)\\n    trace_groups = {}\\n    with open(log_file, 'r', encoding='utf-8', errors='ignore') as f:\\n        for line in f:\\n            line = line.strip()\\n            if not line: continue\\n            \\n            entry = {}\\n            j_start = line.find('{')\\n            if j_start != -1 and line.endswith('}'):\\n                try:\\n                    entry = json.loads(line[j_start:])\\n                except:\\n                    pass\\n            elif '=' in line:\\n                for m in KV_REGEX.findall(line):\\n                    k = m[0]\\n                    v = m[1] if m[1] != '' else m[2]\\n                    if v not in ('null', 'None'):\\n                        entry[k] = v\\n            \\n            trace_id = entry.get('trace_id') or entry.get('requestId')\\n            if trace_id:\\n                trace_groups.setdefault(trace_id, []).append(entry)\\n\\n    traces_found += len(trace_groups)\\n    for tid, entries in trace_groups.items():\\n        # Pass 1:\\n        trace_email = None\\n        trace_user_id = None\\n        for e in entries:\\n            for k in ('lookup_key', 'subject_ref', 'subject_reference', 'email', 'customer_email', 'requester_email'):\\n                val = e.get(k)\\n                if val:\\n                    val = str(val).strip()\\n                    if '@' in val and not trace_email:\\n                        trace_email = val\\n                    if val.startswith('user_') and not trace_user_id:\\n                        trace_user_id = val\\n        if trace_email or trace_user_id:\\n            correlated_rows += 1\\n\\nprint('Total traces:', traces_found, 'Traces with identifiers:', correlated_rows)\\n\\\"\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolSummary":"\"Test trace correlation logic\""}}]}
{"step_index":371,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"RUNNING","created_at":"2026-10-24T18:59:14Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-25T00:29:14+05:30\nTool is running as a background task with task id: 51374649-1a7b-432a-985e-98e8fd1f22c3/task-371\nTask Description: python -c \"\nimport glob, json, re\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nKV_REGEX = re.compile(r'(\\w+)=(?:\\\"([^\\\"]*)\\\"|(\\S+))')\n\nlog_dir = Path(r'C:\\Users\\Pavan\\hackerrank-orchestrate-october26\\dataset\\evidence\\logs')\ntraces_found = 0\ncorrelated_rows = 0\n\nfor log_file in sorted(log_dir.glob('*.log')):\n    # trace_id -> list of raw entries (dict)\n    trace_groups = {}\n    with open(log_file, 'r', encoding='utf-8', errors='ignore') as f:\n        for line in f:\n            line = line.strip()\n            if not line: continue\n            \n            entry = {}\n            j_start = line.find('{')\n            if j_start != -1 and line.endswith('}'):\n                try:\n                    entry = json.loads(line[j_start:])\n                except:\n                    pass\n            elif '=' in line:\n                for m in KV_REGEX.findall(line):\n                    k = m[0]\n                    v = m[1] if m[1] != '' else m[2]\n                    if v not in ('null', 'None'):\n                        entry[k] = v\n            \n            trace_id = entry.get('trace_id') or entry.get('requestId')\n            if trace_id:\n                trace_groups.setdefault(trace_id, []).append(entry)\n\n    traces_found += len(trace_groups)\n    for tid, entries in trace_groups.items():\n        # Pass 1:\n        trace_email = None\n        trace_user_id = None\n        for e in entries:\n            for k in ('lookup_key', 'subject_ref', 'subject_reference', 'email', 'customer_email', 'requester_email'):\n                val = e.get(k)\n                if val:\n                    val = str(val).strip()\n                    if '@' in val and not trace_email:\n                        trace_email = val\n                    if val.startswith('user_') and not trace_user_id:\n                        trace_user_id = val\n        if trace_email or trace_user_id:\n            correlated_rows += 1\n\nprint('Total traces:', traces_found, 'Traces with identifiers:', correlated_rows)\n\"\nTask logs are available at: file:///C:/Users/Pavan/.gemini/antigravity/brain/51374649-1a7b-432a-985e-98e8fd1f22c3/.system_generated/tasks/task-371.log\nYOU MUST TAKE ONE OF THE FOLLOWING TWO ACTIONS: A) either proceed to other relevant work (if any) or, B) simply update the user with a short message (that you have launched the command and will wait for it to finish) and end the turn.\n DO NOTHING ELSE."}
